From 67597023708e1afb993fad2249cc2bf41616f42c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joaco2382 <104966815+Joaco2382@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 19:46:08 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] feat: puppet warp for every MDLV version, with skeleton and
 animations

Puppet image layers only worked for MDLV0021/MDLV0023 and even then were drawn
in their stored (sprite sheet) layout: pieces that bones move into place
floated around (#626, #669, #239), and any other version was rejected.

- PuppetParser reads the .mdl sections in order instead of a fixed layout per
  version: the vertex size comes from the vertex format descriptor (52 bytes
  for 0x01800009, 80 for 0x0180000F), the mesh is located by validating the
  whole vertex + index block (it must end right at MDLS and every index must
  be in range), then the MDLS skeleton (bind transforms relative to the
  parent) and the MDLA animations (one track of keyframes per bone, found by
  validating their layout so version specific padding/event lists are
  skipped).
- PuppetPose applies the object's animation layers (loop, mirror and single
  play modes, rate, blend) to the skeleton and skins the mesh on the CPU
  every frame. Angles are authored with y pointing down, so rotations around
  x and z are flipped for the y-up mesh.
- Like Wallpaper Engine, effects now run on the flat image (their masks are
  painted on it) and the posed mesh only shapes the final draw into the
  scene. Drawing the mesh in the first pass let effects that make the whole
  layer opaque (tint with BLENDMODE 0, used by character outline layers)
  cover everything behind the layer's rectangle, and left effect masks
  misaligned with the posed pieces.
- Face culling is disabled while drawing the mesh (the y flip reverses the
  winding, #620) and a puppet without effects uses its scene space vertices.
- If the skeleton or animations can't be read the mesh is drawn in its bind
  pose; if the mesh can't be read the layer is drawn as the plain image.

Tested with workshop 2791601501 (MDLV0014, three sprite sheet characters),
2327607728 and 2452613331 (MDLV0013) against their preview.gif, plus 20
scenes without puppets (no change beyond run to run noise).
